# Organ Trio Sonata No. 4 in E minor, BWV 528: III. Un poco allegro
# (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a light, quick trio in 3/8. The subject is short and
# pointed (a leap up to E, a falling sigh to D-sharp, then a run of
# sixteenths); the two upper lines answer each other and later run in
# parallel sixteenths, over a pedal in quarter and eighth notes. Not
# fast ("un poco"), but it must dance.
#
# Time signature: 3/8, 97 bars, no upbeat, no repeats (Mutopia
# SonataIV-2.mid, checked against Allegro.ly: the third score in the
# set; the MIDI holds exactly 97 bars).
#
# Tempo: eighth = 112 (dotted quarter about 37), about 2:40. Confirmed
# track times: George Baker (organ, 1976, Apple Music Classical) 2:29,
# about eighth = 117; Roberto Loreggian and Mario Folena (harpsichord
# and flute arrangement) 2:47, about 104. The Mutopia MIDI has eighth =
# 118. Ton Koopman (Teldec, 1995) takes the whole sonata in 9:43, with
# the Andante at 4:38, so his outer movements share 5:05 between them;
# his figure for this one I could not confirm. 112 sits between Baker
# and Loreggian/Folena: lively, and the parallel sixteenths stay clean
# (about 16 frames each).
#
# Structure (my reading of the score; no published bar plan was found):
#   1-8    subject, soprano, E minor, over the pedal.
#   9-16   answer, alto, on B; the soprano runs above it.
#   16-20  the upper lines in sequence without pedal.
#   21-27  E minor, the lines in parallel sixteenths; cadence at 27-28.
#   28-32  falling sequence over a moving pedal.
#   33-43  to G major; cadence at 43.
#   44-51  the subject in the soprano from G (44), sequences.
#   52-59  toward A minor, the lines exchanging figures.
#   60-67  over a pedal in eighths; cadence in A minor at 67.
#   68-74  the subject returns in the soprano, E minor, as at bars 1-7,
#          now with the alto running above and around it.
#   75-79  sequence, both lines in sixteenths over long pedal notes.
#   80-88  bars 21-29 again with the upper lines exchanged.
#   89-97  the close, cadence in E minor.
#
# Plan: one registration through the movement, as in the other two, so
# the upper lines are equal and the level moves only at the main
# cadences, one step at a time; the return of the subject (68) is the
# fullest. The alto's first answer (9-12) is brought forward a little so
# the imitation is heard. Pedal notes below B2 are lifted an octave by
# the converter.

tempo 112 8

voice top 0           # soprano and alto equal
voice mid 0
voice bottom 0        # the pedal at full voice

dyn 1 mf              # bars 1-27: exposition and the E minor section
lead 9-12 mid         # the alto's answer, below the soprano
dyn 28 mp             # bars 28-43: sequences, to the G major cadence
broaden 42 0.95       # bar 42: into the G major cadence
dyn 44 mf             # bars 44-67: the subject from G, on to A minor
broaden 66 0.95       # bar 66: into the A minor cadence
dyn 68 f              # bars 68-97: the subject's return in E minor

rit 4 0.75            # bars 94-97: the final cadence
